   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Jackie Robinson (1919\u20131972) broke Major League Baseball's color barrier on April 15, 1947, with the Brooklyn Dodgers, enduring racism with grace to open pro sports to Black athletes. He was Rookie of the Year, an MVP, and his number 42 is retired by every team."
