   "name": "Who paid for the Emancipation Memorial in Washington?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "The Emancipation Memorial in Washington's Lincoln Park, dedicated in 1876, was funded entirely by formerly enslaved people \u2014 yet its image of Lincoln standing over a kneeling freedman drew Frederick Douglass's private criticism at its own dedication; the debate over it, carried honestly, is part of its record."
